  "notes": "Facts: Shaniwar Wada, Pune; foundation laid by Peshwa Bajirao I in 1730 on a Saturday (completed 1732). Narayanrao became Peshwa at 17 and was killed by Gardi soldiers in Shaniwar Wada on 30 Aug 1773; plot attributed to Raghunathrao / Anandibai. Fire of 27 Feb 1828 burned ~7 days, cause unknown. Legend ('kehte hain'): Anandibai changed 'dhara' (catch) to 'mara' (kill) in the order; 'Kaka mala vachva' cry heard on full-moon nights. No gore: the killing is shown symbolically.",
